KNOWNBUG
negative-range-bit-select1.sv
--bound 1
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.v\[-8\] == 1'b1: PROVED up to bound 1$
^\[main\.p1\] always main\.v\[-7\] == 1'b0: PROVED up to bound 1$
^\[main\.p2\] always main\.v\[7\] == 1'b0: PROVED up to bound 1$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
This crashes with an invariant failure.
1800-2017 11.5.1 permits negative vector range bounds:
"It shall be legal for the ranges of a vector to be a negative number."
A vector declared as [7:-8] has indices -8..7; a bit-select with a
negative (in-range) index such as v[-8] is legal and selects the
corresponding bit (here the least-significant bit).
